<!DOCTYPE html><html  lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Finance Payment Request Follow-Ups workflow | StackOS</title><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_vzy7sc.png"><meta name="twitter:image:src" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_vzy7sc.png"><meta property="og:image" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_vzy7sc.png"><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"><meta name="twitter:image:width" content="1200"><meta property="og:image:height" content="600"><meta name="twitter:image:height" content="600"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/entry.z7ALz4wj.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/_slug_.P4W8Caq7.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/GeneratedVisual.Cf-hdjOs.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/WorkflowMap.DZrXaqny.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/CatalogCard.CZo9PXiI.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/LibraryFrame.CD2pOTex.css" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/fonts/manrope-latin-variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous"><link rel="preload" as="fetch" crossorigin="anonymous" href="/library/workflows/finance-payment-request-followups/_payload.json?aa8e47a4-cf64-43ed-8aa2-6473b185d6eb"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/BT73oLzS.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/nWp2neeF.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/LP-lSYvf.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/B1N7hItV.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/8-IjujsF.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/Dbua9CwJ.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/DIYlYVLR.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/B6FA65gX.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/CBNv9QJs.js"><script type="module" src="/_nuxt/BT73oLzS.js" crossorigin></script><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/stackos-icon.png"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/images/stackos-icon.png"><link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="StackOS Library" href="/feed.xml"><meta name="description" content="A safe external follow-up or settlement decision record. Every invoice is suppressed, exception-bound, or eligible for one instructed contact through the selected Stripe resend or SMTP…"><meta name="theme-color" content="#090b10"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="Finance Payment Request Follow-Ups workflow | StackOS"><meta property="og:description" content="A safe external follow-up or settlement decision record. Every invoice is suppressed, exception-bound, or eligible for one instructed contact through the selected Stripe resend or SMTP…"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Finance Payment Request Follow-Ups workflow | StackOS"><meta name="twitter:description" content="A safe external follow-up or settlement decision record. Every invoice is suppressed, exception-bound, or eligible for one instructed contact through the selected Stripe resend or SMTP…"><meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1"><link rel="canonical" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/workflows/finance-payment-request-followups/"><meta property="og:url" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/workflows/finance-payment-request-followups/"><meta property="og:site_name" content="StackOS"><script id="unhead:payload" type="application/json">{"titleTemplate":"%s | StackOS"}</script></head><body><div id="__nuxt"><!--[--><div id="top" class="site library-site" data-v-58a46588 data-v-e230b581><a class="skip-link" href="#main" data-v-e230b581>Skip to content</a><header class="site-header" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell site-header__inner"><a href="/" class="brand" aria-label="StackOS home"><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt width="36" height="36"><span>StackOS</span><small>Work, organized</small></a><nav class="site-nav site-nav--desktop" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav><details class="mobile-menu"><summary role="button" aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-controls="site-navigation"><span></span><span></span></summary><nav id="site-navigation" class="site-nav site-nav--mobile" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav></details></div></header><div class="library-nav" aria-label="Library sections" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell library-nav__inner" data-v-e230b581><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Workflows</a><a href="/library/agents/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Agents</a><a href="/library/orchestrators/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Orchestrators</a><a href="/library/integrations/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Integrations</a><a href="/library/articles/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Articles</a></div></div><main id="main" class="library-main" data-v-e230b581><nav class="library-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-v-e230b581 data-v-59391fa3><div class="shell" data-v-59391fa3><ol data-v-59391fa3><!--[--><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Home</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Library</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Workflows</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a aria-current="page" href="/library/workflows/finance-payment-request-followups/" class="router-link-active router-link-exact-active" data-v-59391fa3>Finance Payment Request Follow-Ups</a></li><!--]--></ol></div></nav><!--[--><section class="detail-hero" data-v-58a46588><div class="shell detail-hero__grid" data-v-58a46588><div data-v-58a46588><p class="library-kicker" data-v-58a46588>Solo entrepreneurs reviewing Stripe invoice follow-ups or reconciling a customer payment already received / finance</p><h1 data-v-58a46588>Finance Payment Request Follow-Ups</h1><p class="detail-hero__lede" data-v-58a46588>A safe external follow-up or settlement decision record. Every invoice is suppressed, exception-bound, or eligible for one instructed contact through the selected Stripe resend or SMTP…</p><div class="detail-tags" data-v-58a46588><span data-v-58a46588>9 stages</span><span data-v-58a46588>2 specialist agents</span><span data-v-58a46588>Connection required</span></div></div><div class="generated-visual generated-visual--workflow detail-hero__visual" style="--visual-color:#d9ff63;" role="img" aria-label="A complete plan you can follow. Finance Payment Request Follow-Ups. From request to result." data-v-58a46588 data-v-9361e887><header class="generated-visual__header" data-v-9361e887><div data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887>From request to result</span><strong data-v-9361e887>A complete plan you can follow.</strong></div><small data-v-9361e887>Visible plan</small></header><div class="generated-visual__lane" aria-hidden="true" data-v-9361e887><div class="visual-node visual-node--clients" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Start in your AI</span><div class="client-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/openai.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Codex</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/claude.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Claude</b></span><span class="client-chip" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/gemini.webp" alt="" width="34" height="34" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>Gemini</b></span><!--]--></div></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--stackos" data-v-9361e887><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt="" width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-9361e887><strong data-v-9361e887>StackOS</strong><small data-v-9361e887>Builds the plan</small></div><i class="visual-connector" data-v-9361e887><span data-v-9361e887></span></i><div class="visual-node visual-node--outcome" data-v-9361e887><span class="visual-node__label" data-v-9361e887>Visible stages</span><div class="outcome-list" data-v-9361e887><!--[--><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>1</b> Plan</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>2</b> Do</span><span data-v-9361e887><b data-v-9361e887>3</b> Check</span><!--]--></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-body" data-v-58a46588><div class="detail-body__narrow" data-v-58a46588><p class="eyebrow" data-v-58a46588>The problem</p><h2 data-v-58a46588>A solo operator needs overdue-payment follow-ups and a safe way to reconcile money already received, but a generic reminder or an unverified paid mark can duplicate a payment or misstate what a customer owes.</h2><p class="detail-body__intro" data-v-58a46588>An agent can re-check bounded provider lifecycle and received-payment evidence against the external record, leaving collection judgment, allocation choices, customer terms, and material settlement approval with the operator.</p></div><div class="shell experience-grid" data-v-58a46588><article data-v-58a46588><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark" data-v-58a46588>What you do</p><ol data-v-58a46588><!--[--><li data-v-58a46588>Request a collections check for a review window, or report that a customer wired or otherwise paid money directly; the agent resolves the selected external scope, invoice mappings, recent contacts and reminder policy.</li><li data-v-58a46588>Review exceptions, active promises, the independently prepared eligible set, or the exact received-payment match/allocation.</li><li data-v-58a46588>Specify the contact route and requested follow-up or use documented settings; existing Stripe approvals still apply to Stripe actions.</li><!--]--></ol></article><article data-v-58a46588><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark" data-v-58a46588>What the agent does</p><ol data-v-58a46588><!--[--><li data-v-58a46588>Read bounded Stripe invoice and invoice-payment lifecycle evidence plus the selected external follow-up or received-payment state.</li><li data-v-58a46588>For a settlement-only occurrence, match one source and allocation, obtain independent review, then report/attach it or mark the exact verified full remaining balance as paid out of band.</li><li data-v-58a46588>Suppress every paid, voided, disputed, paused, corrected, active-promise, mismatch, or unresolved received-payment case before any send action.</li><li data-v-58a46588>Have the control reviewer challenge the eligibility/suppression or settlement decision, then use the selected action&#39;s grant and existing authority; Stripe mutations retain their owner gates.</li><li data-v-58a46588>Write safe outcome and recovery refs to the selected external backend.</li><!--]--></ol></article></div><div class="detail-body__narrow detail-space" data-v-58a46588><p class="eyebrow" data-v-58a46588>When this workflow helps</p><h2 data-v-58a46588>A reusable method, adapted to the request.</h2><ul class="detail-list" data-v-58a46588><!--[--><li data-v-58a46588>A bounded set of sent/open external invoices needs lifecycle-aware follow-up evaluation.</li><li data-v-58a46588>A customer wired money, paid directly, or paid separately through Stripe and the received payment must be matched to one invoice without charging the customer.</li><!--]--></ul></div><div class="shell readiness-grid" data-v-58a46588><article data-v-58a46588><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark" data-v-58a46588>Before it starts</p><h3 data-v-58a46588>Connection required</h3><ul data-v-58a46588><!--[--><li data-v-58a46588>A selected workspace and review window; resolve follow-up rules/history/reminder ownership for followup-only, or the received-payment source/allocation for settlement-only</li><li data-v-58a46588>Restricted Stripe invoice/payment read access</li><li data-v-58a46588>An operator instruction or documented follow-up settings selecting the route; SMTP credentials when smtp-email is selected, and existing Stripe approval gates for Stripe mutations</li><!--]--></ul></article><article data-v-58a46588><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark" data-v-58a46588>What proves it worked</p><h3 data-v-58a46588>Evidence, not a success claim.</h3><ul data-v-58a46588><!--[--><li data-v-58a46588>Safe invoice/payment/external-follow-up refs and suppression, settlement, or eligibility state</li><li data-v-58a46588>Control-reviewer, applicable Stripe owner approval, source/allocation, and external-record version refs</li><li data-v-58a46588>Action-call and external-write proof refs for any approved settlement or resend</li><!--]--></ul></article></div><div class="shell workflow-showcase" data-v-58a46588><div class="library-section__heading" data-v-58a46588><div data-v-58a46588><p class="eyebrow" data-v-58a46588>Workflow path</p><h2 data-v-58a46588>The reusable stages of the work.</h2></div><p data-v-58a46588>A real run expands these stages around the request, context, selected tools, approvals, and dependencies.</p></div><section class="workflow-map" style="--workflow-color:#8ea6ff;" aria-labelledby="workflow-map-title" data-v-58a46588 data-v-110563eb><header data-v-110563eb><span class="status-dot" data-v-110563eb></span><strong id="workflow-map-title" data-v-110563eb>9 ordered workflow stages</strong></header><ol aria-label="Workflow stages" data-v-110563eb><!--[--><li data-workflow-stage data-v-110563eb><span data-v-110563eb>01</span><div data-v-110563eb><h3 data-v-110563eb>Preflight Follow-Up Scope</h3><p data-v-110563eb>Resolve the review scope and only the setup applicable to the selected occurrence mode.</p></div><small data-v-110563eb>Passes to next stage</small></li><li data-workflow-stage data-v-110563eb><span data-v-110563eb>02</span><div data-v-110563eb><h3 data-v-110563eb>Read Bounded Invoice Lifecycle</h3><p data-v-110563eb>Retrieve bounded Stripe lifecycle evidence and, only when selected, retain customer reply evidence externally.</p></div><small data-v-110563eb>Passes to next stage</small></li><li data-workflow-stage data-v-110563eb><span data-v-110563eb>03</span><div data-v-110563eb><h3 data-v-110563eb>Prepare Received-Payment Settlement</h3><p data-v-110563eb>For settlement-only work, read and match one already-received Stripe or direct-bank payment to one invoice without creating a payment or moving money.…</p></div><small data-v-110563eb>Passes to next stage</small></li><li data-workflow-stage data-v-110563eb><span data-v-110563eb>04</span><div data-v-110563eb><h3 data-v-110563eb>Independently Review Settlement Route</h3><p data-v-110563eb>Have the control reviewer challenge the current external source, allocation, match, route, and owner approval before a settlement mutation.</p></div><small data-v-110563eb>Passes to next stage</small></li><li data-workflow-stage data-v-110563eb><span data-v-110563eb>05</span><div data-v-110563eb><h3 data-v-110563eb>Apply Owner-Approved Settlement</h3><p data-v-110563eb>Run at most the one selected owner-gated Stripe settlement action route and immediately reconcile provider/external state without collecting money.</p></div><small data-v-110563eb>Passes to next stage</small></li><li data-workflow-stage data-v-110563eb><span data-v-110563eb>06</span><div data-v-110563eb><h3 data-v-110563eb>Suppress Ineligible Follow-Ups</h3><p data-v-110563eb>Apply required lifecycle and external-state suppression before eligibility is considered.</p></div><small data-v-110563eb>Passes to next stage</small></li><li data-workflow-stage data-v-110563eb><span data-v-110563eb>07</span><div data-v-110563eb><h3 data-v-110563eb>Independently Review Eligible Set</h3><p data-v-110563eb>Review lifecycle/suppression and the requested contact under the selected route&#39;s existing authority.</p></div><small data-v-110563eb>Passes to next stage</small></li><li data-workflow-stage data-v-110563eb><span data-v-110563eb>08</span><div data-v-110563eb><h3 data-v-110563eb>Send Requested Follow-Up</h3><p data-v-110563eb>Submit the requested contact through its selected action and preserve truthful transport outcome evidence.</p></div><small data-v-110563eb>Passes to next stage</small></li><li data-workflow-stage data-v-110563eb><span data-v-110563eb>09</span><div data-v-110563eb><h3 data-v-110563eb>Record External Outcome And Handoff</h3><p data-v-110563eb>Update only the selected external backend with safe status/proof refs and hand off relevant preparation work.</p></div><small data-v-110563eb>Verified outcome</small></li><!--]--></ol></section></div><div class="detail-body__narrow" style="margin-top:88px;" data-v-58a46588><!--[--><p class="eyebrow" data-v-58a46588>Safe stopping and recovery</p><h2 data-v-58a46588>Useful even when the whole path cannot run.</h2><ul class="detail-list" data-v-58a46588><!--[--><li data-v-58a46588>Stop contact when the selected route is unavailable or the instruction/settings are ambiguous; existing Stripe action approvals remain required.</li><li data-v-58a46588>Stop after settlement preparation or review when no matching owner settlement approval is recorded.</li><li data-v-58a46588>Stop with a safe recovery ref when delivery or settlement outcome is uncertain.</li><!--]--><!--[--><li data-v-58a46588>If invoice lifecycle or promise state is incomplete, suppress by default and record an external exception.</li><li data-v-58a46588>Reconcile unknown or partial contact outcomes through the selected transport&#39;s audit and retained evidence; an open invoice does not resolve SMTP acceptance. Do not switch routes or blindly retry.</li><li data-v-58a46588>If a PaymentRecord report, payment attachment, or paid-out-of-band mark is unknown, re-read the known provider object and selected external record before any retry; never create a new source identity or idempotency key to bypass uncertainty.</li><!--]--></ul><!--]--><!--[--><p class="eyebrow detail-space" data-v-58a46588>Documented follow-on work</p><h2 data-v-58a46588>The next workflow is conditional, not hidden.</h2><div class="handoff-list" data-v-58a46588><!--[--><a href="/library/workflows/finance-bookkeeping-close/" class="" data-v-58a46588><span data-v-58a46588>conditional</span><strong data-v-58a46588>Finance Bookkeeping Preparation and Reconciliation</strong><p data-v-58a46588>Observed invoice/payment lifecycle or a one-source/one-allocation settlement needs a prepared/unposted external reconciliation entry.</p></a><a href="/library/workflows/finance-cashflow-management/" class="" data-v-58a46588><span data-v-58a46588>conditional</span><strong data-v-58a46588>Finance Cashflow Management</strong><p data-v-58a46588>A reviewed follow-up status changes forecast assumptions, or a verified actual receipt needs a once-only external cashflow handoff under the selected policy.</p></a><!--]--></div><!--]--><!--[--><p class="eyebrow detail-space" data-v-58a46588>Specialists inside this workflow</p><h2 data-v-58a46588>Clear roles for each part of the job.</h2><div class="detail-link-grid" data-v-58a46588><!--[--><a href="/library/agents/stackos-finance-billing-collections-operator/" class="" data-v-58a46588><span data-v-58a46588>Agent</span><strong data-v-58a46588>Finance Billing and Collections Operator</strong><b aria-hidden="true" data-v-58a46588>→</b></a><a href="/library/agents/stackos-finance-control-reviewer/" class="" data-v-58a46588><span data-v-58a46588>Agent</span><strong data-v-58a46588>Finance Control Reviewer</strong><b aria-hidden="true" data-v-58a46588>→</b></a><!--]--></div><!--]--><!--[--><p class="eyebrow detail-space" data-v-58a46588>Connected work</p><h2 data-v-58a46588>Built to use the tools you already have.</h2><div class="detail-tags detail-tags--paper" data-v-58a46588><!--[--><span data-v-58a46588>Smtp</span><span data-v-58a46588>Imap</span><span data-v-58a46588>Stripe</span><!--]--></div><!--]--></div></section><section class="related-section" data-v-58a46588><div class="shell" data-v-58a46588><div class="library-section__heading" data-v-58a46588><div data-v-58a46588><p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark" data-v-58a46588>Keep exploring</p><h2 data-v-58a46588>Related workflows.</h2></div><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-58a46588>See all 36 →</a></div><div class="library-grid" data-v-58a46588><!--[--><a href="/library/workflows/finance-bookkeeping-close/" class="catalog-card" style="--card-color:#8ea6ff;" data-v-58a46588 data-v-661e3dea><div class="catalog-card__visual" aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea><!--[--><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><!--]--></div><div class="catalog-card__meta" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>workflow</span><b data-v-661e3dea>finance</b></div><h3 data-v-661e3dea>Finance Bookkeeping Preparation and Reconciliation</h3><p data-v-661e3dea>A reviewed, externally recorded close packet marked prepared/unposted, with matched and exception refs that can be handed to later workflows.</p><div class="catalog-card__footer" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>5 stages</span><b aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea>↗</b></div></a><a href="/library/workflows/finance-cashflow-management/" class="catalog-card" style="--card-color:#8ea6ff;" data-v-58a46588 data-v-661e3dea><div class="catalog-card__visual" aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea><!--[--><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><!--]--></div><div class="catalog-card__meta" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>workflow</span><b data-v-661e3dea>finance</b></div><h3 data-v-661e3dea>Finance Cashflow Management</h3><p data-v-661e3dea>A dated external thirteen-week forecast packet with safe evidence/proof refs, uncertainty, exception state, and tax-estimate handoff readiness.</p><div class="catalog-card__footer" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>4 stages</span><b aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea>↗</b></div></a><a href="/library/workflows/finance-payment-request/" class="catalog-card" style="--card-color:#8ea6ff;" data-v-58a46588 data-v-661e3dea><div class="catalog-card__visual" aria-hidden="true" data-v-661e3dea><!--[--><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><i data-v-661e3dea></i><span data-v-661e3dea></span><!--]--></div><div class="catalog-card__meta" data-v-661e3dea><span data-v-661e3dea>workflow</span><b data-v-661e3dea>finance</b></div><h3 data-v-661e3dea>Finance Payment Request</h3><p data-v-661e3dea>One external 